+.. _installation-method-rocm:
+
+AMD GPUs with ROCm
+------------------
+
+The Newton workflows run on AMD Instinct GPUs with PyTorch and Warp built for ROCm. This setup has been tested on
+AMD Instinct MI300X (``gfx942``) on Linux x86_64. Isaac Sim, the OV backends, and the Isaac RTX and OVRTX renderers
+need NVIDIA GPUs and are not available on this path.
+
+Warp runs graph-capturing code eagerly on HIP devices, so ``use_cuda_graph`` settings have no effect there. Warp
+textures are not supported on HIP devices, so the Newton Warp renderer cannot load textured meshes.
+
+Create a Python 3.12 environment in the Isaac Lab checkout and install PyTorch together with the matching ROCm SDK
+from AMD's package index. The index path selects the GPU family, here ``gfx94X-dcgpu`` for MI300:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+   uv venv --python 3.12 .venv
+   source .venv/bin/activate
+   uv pip install --index-url https://pypi.org/simple \
+      --extra-index-url https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl/gfx94X-dcgpu/ \
+      torch==2.11.0+rocm7.13.0 torchvision==0.26.0+rocm7.13.0 "rocm[libraries,devel]==7.13.0"
+   export ROCM_PATH=$(rocm-sdk path --root)
+   export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$ROCM_PATH/lib
+
+Keep ``ROCM_PATH`` and ``LD_LIBRARY_PATH`` set whenever you run Isaac Lab: Warp compiles kernels at runtime and
+looks up the ROCm headers and libraries through them.
+
+Build Warp with the HIP backend from AMD's Warp repository for your GPU architecture. Build on a host without a CUDA
+Toolkit, which the Warp build would select instead of ROCm:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+   git clone https://github.com/AMD-Ecosystem/warp.git ../warp-rocm
+   git -C ../warp-rocm checkout ac540f595ff5763a374c113d77e4111a1d4791bd
+   (cd ../warp-rocm && python build_lib.py --rocm-path "$ROCM_PATH" --hip-arch=gfx942 --no-use-libmathdx)
+
+Install Isaac Lab with overrides that keep the ROCm builds of PyTorch and Warp. ``--no-sources`` drops the CUDA
+PyTorch index that the project selects for PyTorch, so the workspace packages are listed explicitly:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+   cat > rocm-overrides.txt <<EOF
+   torch==2.11.0+rocm7.13.0
+   torchvision==0.26.0+rocm7.13.0
+   warp-lang @ file://$(realpath ../warp-rocm)
+   EOF
+   uv pip install --no-sources --override rocm-overrides.txt \
+      --index https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl/gfx94X-dcgpu/ \
+      -e . -e source/isaaclab -e source/isaaclab_assets -e source/isaaclab_contrib \
+      -e source/isaaclab_experimental -e source/isaaclab_newton -e source/isaaclab_ov \
+      -e source/isaaclab_physx -e source/isaaclab_ppisp -e source/isaaclab_rl -e source/isaaclab_tasks \
+      -e source/isaaclab_tasks_experimental -e source/isaaclab_visualizers
+
+Then run a Newton workflow from the activated environment:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+   isaaclab train --rl_library rsl_rl --task Isaac-Cartpole-Direct physics=newton_mjwarp
+
