From 03bb17b08290babb82d18bb3e2adb25ff1a5194c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Daily <jeff.daily@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:01:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [ROCm] Keep the GPU info recorder metadata unchanged

The previous commit added a `hip_version` metadata entry to the GPU info benchmark recorder on ROCm builds of PyTorch. `TestGPUInfoRecorder::test_get_data_returns_measurement_data` expects exactly four metadata entries, and the recorder already falls back to `torch.cuda.memory_allocated` and an `Unknown` CUDA version without NVML or `nvidia-smi`, so drop the extra entry and its changelog bullet.

This change was prepared with the help of an AI coding agent.

Test Plan:

On an AMD Instinct MI300X (gfx942) with PyTorch 2.11.0+rocm7.13.0:

```bash
python -m pytest source/isaaclab/test/benchmark/test_recorders.py
python tools/changelog/cli.py check upstream/main
```
---
 source/isaaclab/changelog.d/rocm-graph-capture.added.rst     | 1 -
 .../isaaclab/isaaclab/benchmark/recorders/record_gpu_info.py | 5 -----
 2 files changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/isaaclab/changelog.d/rocm-graph-capture.added.rst b/source/isaaclab/changelog.d/rocm-graph-capture.added.rst
index b2d3e8e73..b1c73c9e1 100644
--- a/source/isaaclab/changelog.d/rocm-graph-capture.added.rst
+++ b/source/isaaclab/changelog.d/rocm-graph-capture.added.rst
@@ -1,4 +1,3 @@
 * Added :func:`~isaaclab.utils.warp.utils.supports_graph_capture` to check whether Warp can capture CUDA graphs on a
   device, and :func:`~isaaclab.test.utils.skip_without_graph_capture` to skip the capture part of a test on devices
